  "summary": "I added a \"Lights off\" button below the canvas in `src/main.ts`, and typecheck passes. I haven't run it in a browser, so the night brightness is untested.\n\n- **Button:** Clicking it switches to a dim, bluish night look and relabels it \"Lights on\". Clicking again restores the warm lighting. Night mode lowers the ambient, hemisphere and spotlight levels and darkens the background. The face light stays on and the interior light is only halved, so the face stays readable.\n- **State:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` is set every frame to `{ lightsOn, pendulumAngleDeg }`. The angle is the pendulum's signed angle from vertical in degrees, which stays within ±0.17 rad (about ±9.7°)."
